  "name": "biscuit-swift",
  "description": "A Swift implementation of the Biscuit authorization token specification, facilitating decentralized validation and cryptographic offline attenuation. It features a Datalog-based logic engine for evaluating access policies and constraints, coupled with a type-safe Swift DSL for token construction and verification. The framework leverages Ed25519 and Secp256r1 for signature chains and Protocol Buffers for efficient binary serialization.",
